cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software and evidence package, please cite the archived release associated with this repository version."
title: "Supplementary Software 1: MFP-Score, OPR, and Source-Grounded Evidence Workflow for Monolithic MOF Formation"
authors:
  - family-names: "Wei"
    given-names: "Jinnan"
    affiliation: "Yusuf Hamied Department of Chemistry, University of Cambridge"
  - family-names: "Wheatley"
    given-names: "Andrew E. H."
    affiliation: "Yusuf Hamied Department of Chemistry, University of Cambridge"
    email: "aehw2@cam.ac.uk"
version: "v1.1.0"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/poiuy1v1/paper2-mfp-score-opr-prototype"
abstract: >-
  MIT-licensed supplementary software and source-grounded evidence package for
  monolithic MOF prioritization. The release contains the synthetic-curated
  MFP-Score/OPR demonstration, a 49-record condition-level evidence registry,
  descriptive manuscript-table generation, a nullable registry-to-model
  projection adapter, checksums, and validation reports. The evidence layer is
  descriptive and is explicitly excluded from MFP scoring, OPR ranking,
  classifier training, performance metrics, and synthetic imputation.
keywords:
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - monolithic MOF
  - MFP-Score
  - optimal processing route
  - source-grounded evidence
  - materials informatics
  - reproducible workflow
